"Liora was a human woman of Earth, reborn in this world as a magpie hatched from an egg."
"Her Earth memories were locked until Lucien's mind probe tore them open; they still hurt."
"She recalls cold, abusive parents, a burning building, gunfire, and a crowd under sirens."
"She lived two years as a plain magpie until Renir, sealed in his gem, gave her the System."
"She stole Renir's gem from a wagon of Order mages when a corrupted boar attacked it."
"She has been Common Magpie, Duskwing Magpie, Starfeather Corvid and Lumenwing Aethral."
"Her species now is Prismfeather Dracoryx, a secret evolution; she is Level 33 or a little more."
"She must reach Level 50 and pay an unknown sum of glimmerstones to evolve again."
"She hoards some 1,745 glimmerstones; Glimmerlust at Legend turns each into power and speed."
"Skills: Resonance Mimicry II, Meteor Impact, Prism Air Slash II, Decoy Fade II, Raptor Lunge."
"Skills: Mana Conversion, Poison Shot, Holy Light, Wind Blast, Purify at Legend, Featherflash."
"Skills: Aegis Cyclone, a wind shield; and Theft, still at Basic, which she is training now."
"Traits: Prismatic Twilight Vision II, which sees mana; Treasure Sense; Aerial Agility at Legend."
"Traits: Nightveil II, Inventory, Magpie Disguise, Ailment Resistance, Fluid Flight."
"Traits: Sound Resistance, Predator of the Deep, and Prismfeather Mantle, which unmakes spells."
"She has an Inventory, which no monster should; her greed forced the System to grant it."
"Her Inventory holds a shark matriarch's glimmercore, one gold coin, and an unexamined orb."
"The orb was left by a pool of living corruption she purified to death in Lucien's island lab."
"Lucien knows she is a reborn human of Earth, and covets what she knows."
"She has fallen out with Renir: he called her stupid for telling his brother Aenir everything."
"Now, near winter's end, she is in the capital of a small desert kingdom southwest of the Navaru."
"She works with Aenir to restore the kingdom's dried river with the antkin's water mana crystals."
"She would rather trade with the antkin for the crystals than steal them."
"She has mapped much of the antkin anthill, and refuses to hand Aenir the map."
"She trains Theft robbing rich, grasping bureaucrats on Aenir's list, paid in shinies."
"Tonight she means to steal a courtship gem shown off at a rich man's evening party."
